findings:
  - id: AOOSR-R1-BLOCKER-001
    severity: blocker
    title: Git replacement objects are not disabled
    evidence:
      - GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS is absent from the literal environment
      - --no-replace-objects is absent from all Git invocations
      - an independent temporary bare-repository reproduction showed that git_cat_file_blob_of_a_fixed_OID_returned_refs_replace_bytes_by_default
      - the same reproduction returned the original OID bytes only with GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1
      - no VCPToolBox command was used for the reproduction
    impact: >
      A literal object ID does not guarantee that Git reads the original object
      bytes or original tree semantics while replacement refs remain active.
      The sealed-object claim is therefore not established by the current
      command envelope.
    required_disposition:
      - bind GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1 in the empty execution environment
      - or bind the equivalent global no-replace option to every Git invocation
      - add a deterministic negative test proving replacement refs cannot alter any observed object

  - id: AOOSR-R1-BLOCKER-002
    severity: blocker
    title: No hash-bound executable runner or scanner is included in the review unit
    evidence:
      - no runner path or runner SHA-256 is declared
      - no scanner path or scanner SHA-256 is declared
      - the NUL-safe protected-name filter is described only in prose
      - environment clearing, scalar capture, digest comparison, output-byte accounting, receipt serialization and finalizer dispatch are not represented by reviewed executable bytes
      - Section 6 A would authorize a later implementation that has not itself received independent review
    impact: >
      The document fixes desired Git command text but cannot prove that the
      actual execution process performs only those commands, suppresses every
      output, handles every failure and signal, or invokes the finalizer
      correctly. The most security-sensitive part of the run remains outside
      the hash-bound review surface.
    required_disposition:
      - add a deterministic runner and scanner as hash-bound review subjects
      - make the runner reject any command inventory or constant drift
      - add offline synthetic fixtures for success, protected-name substitution, extra Git call, output leak and cleanup failure
      - perform a fresh independent review of the complete package plus executable subjects

  - id: AOOSR-R1-BLOCKER-003
    severity: blocker
    title: Path ownership, receipt creation and finalizer semantics are not atomic or complete
    evidence:
      - the canonical VCPToolBox root is tested as a directory but is not rejected when it is itself a symlink
      - the final receipt preexistence check is separated from the later write and no O_EXCL plus O_NOFOLLOW mechanism is bound
      - creation of temporary_result is not specified
      - the finalizer treats a missing temporary_result as cleanup failure
      - signal and interruption paths that must trigger the finalizer are not bound
    impact: >
      A path can change after the precheck, the final receipt writer can race
      with a newly created file or symlink, and failures after run-root creation
      do not have a fully specified cleanup path. The package cannot yet prove
      exclusive ownership or complete fail-closed cleanup.
    required_disposition:
      - reject a symlink canonical root and bind canonical realpath expectations
      - create the final receipt with an exclusive no-follow primitive
      - specify exactly when and how temporary_result is created
      - bind finalizer behavior for success, ordinary failure, interruption and signal paths
      - add adversarial race and residue tests to the reviewed runner

